          "type": "intro",
          "title": "A Raisin in the Sun (1959)",
          "body": "Lorraine Hansberry's landmark play opened on Broadway on March 11, 1959, becoming the first play by a Black woman ever produced there. It transformed American drama, blending naturalism, lyricism, and political clarity into a portrait of a Black family on Chicago's South Side reaching for the dream of a home of their own.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A Raisin in the Sun</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lorraine Hansberry, 1959</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"180\" width=\"860\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#2d1b4e\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Premiere</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">March 11, 1959 — Ethel Barrymore Theatre, Broadway</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">First play by a Black woman on Broadway</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hansberry was 28 years old</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"400\" width=\"860\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#1e3a5f\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"450\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Younger Family</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"490\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Three generations in a cramped South Side apartment</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"525\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Awaiting a $10,000 life insurance check</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"560\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Each member carries a different deferred dream</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"640\" width=\"860\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#1f3d2f\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"690\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cultural Earthquake</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"730\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ran 530 performances; New York Drama Critics' Circle Award</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"765\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">First Black playwright and youngest American to win</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Made the civil rights struggle a Broadway subject</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"880\" width=\"860\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#4a2545\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"930\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Why It Endures</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Family drama + political testimony + poetic title</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1005\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A Black play that refuses the white gaze as final judge</text></svg>",
            "caption": "A Raisin in the Sun overview"
          }
